From dbf462438938fe0d41d420b983715e92b36265e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:21:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-125: the design surface checked against VS / Blend
 / WinForms -- Alt no longer reparents a free move, the wheel zooms about the
 pointer, Esc cancels a drag (0.125.0)

From the manuals check (EastSun 20261001):
- Alt meant two things: VS "pressing and holding the ALT key during drag move/resize" = no
  snapping, Blend "press Alt before releasing" = reparent -- a move held with Alt from the press,
  let go over a Panel, was moved INTO it. Now Alt held from the press = no snapping only; Alt
  pressed during the drag (it was up at some moment) and held at the release = reparent.
- the wheel zoom keeps the point under the pointer (zoomAt; what was under it used to drift away)
- a left / top handle dragged past the opposite edge: the size stopped at 2 px but the edge went
  on and the component slid away -- deltaStyle now stops that edge too (groups as well)
- Esc during a drag / a resize / a rubber band = cancelled, everything back, nothing written
  (it used to select the parent and the release still wrote the move)
- a component placed from the toolbox lands on the grid when snapping to it is on (XD "an
  element tends to align with the closest ... gridlines when you drag it onto the artboard")
- Ctrl+A leaves out the ones hidden in the designer and the locked ones (as the rubber band does);
  Tab skips the hidden ones
Tests: probe -- Alt held from the press = no reparentDrop, Esc = back and no edit, the left handle
past the right edge keeps the right edge, a grid placement lands on multiples of 8; the reparent,
wheel zoom, Ctrl+A and Alt layer checks still pass (the new Alt test puts back whatever its
Alt+press picked). run_all 3/3 layers (lib 168, smoke 198).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
